A||||5||FieroPerformance||Swapped in 120 mph speedo, how do I add an oil pressure gauge?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||11-13-2001||04:32 PM||||I put a 120 mph speedo cluster into my 85 GT. I want to mount an oil pressure gauge and a voltage meter on the pillar. Is there an easy way to wire these into the existing wires that are in the dash?<P>Has anyone else done it, if so how? Plus, where I can find some cool round gauges?<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroPerformance||11-13-2001||04:59 PM||||What kind of gauge should I use? Mechanical or electric? Also, I need to find some 2 1/16" round gauges. Preferably black face, white letters, red needle. Do they offer gauges that light up red like the fiero dash? <P>Thanks.<BR>-Charlie<p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||11-13-2001||05:22 PM||||i still haven't hooked up my oil pressure, but i have it and a voltmeter in round guage holders attatched on the right side of my main guage panel. i used electrical guages 'cause it seemed easier than running an oil line to the front of the car. auto meter. i'd have to walk out to my car 'cause i don't remember what color the needle is but for light they give you a red and green light cover to tint the light. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||11-13-2001||05:27 PM||||Here's a link to info posted awhile back about adding the stock rally guages to an 85 -- which wasn't wired for them from the factory.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||PaulJK||11-14-2001||06:53 AM||||I'm in the process of replacing ALL my instruments - check out <A HREF="http://www.egauges.com" TARGET=_blank>www.egauges.com</A>  - they have a good selection. North hollywood speedometer (www.nhspeedometer.com) sells VDO and others and Will Even Customize The Faces ! I only can speak to the oil press. The easiest way to do this is to get a VDO gauge that accepts the 90 ohm sender - you will not have to change the sender because the fiero factory sender is 90 ohm. NOT ALL VDO GAUGES are 90 ohm compatible - verify this when you buy the gauge ! If you use a gauge that requires another sender, the factory sender is easy to replace BUT BE ADVISED of 2 things - (1) the factory sender will bypass a faulty fuel pump relay & allow the car to run if the fuel pump relay fails; and(2)the factory sender will shutdown the fuel pump if oil press. goes to zero. Replace the factory sender & lose these (2) features - no big deal but be aware of this.<P>When you connected your speedo - Did you keep the factory speedometer buffer and hook up to the brown wire (feeding the ECM and Cruise control) ?||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||11-14-2001||03:49 PM||||if yor car is a 86+ maybe even a 85 the wiringis already there, just lookf for the plug when you pull apart the radio trim and everyting, it is around there somehetre, look<P>Kyle||||reg||1
